#!/bin/bash
# land-mail-gmail.sh — two things Mail was missing. A trail now folds its old
# messages to one tappable line and expands on click, the way every mail client
# does; and every folder gets a search bar, filtered on the server across
# sender, recipients, subject and body. Desktop and phone, one component each.
#
# BACKEND + FRONTEND. Push, and Railway + Vercel ship it.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-react ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

NEEDS="A trail folds, and the mailbox can be searched"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! Working tree is dirty. Commit or stash first:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF

WANT="51f88f344fe5a23b0737afd5908327c8097d463f7794cba1737668053762b43d"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== API gates"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/mail
cd ..

echo "== web gates"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/mail together-city-react/src/features/mail together-city-react/src/index.css
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A trail folds, and the mailbox can be searched

Two things the owner found missing, both of which every mail client has.

ONE: THE TRAIL FOLDS.

collapse.ts has held the rule since the day trails existed — the newest message
open, the one you clicked open, anything unread open, everything else a line
you can tap — with its own tests, in its own file, so the rule could be tested
apart from a component. Nothing ever called it. MessageView rendered every
message in the trail in full, oldest first, so a reply that arrived this
morning sat under four screens of yesterday.

The rule is unchanged; this is the row it always described. A folded message
shows initials, the sender, one line of preview and a date, and the whole row
is the button because on a phone the whole row is what a thumb aims at. The
preview comes from the SAME text the open message renders — quoted history and
the city footer already stripped — so the line and the body can never say two
different things. The server's own `snippet` would have been wrong here: it is
the raw body's first characters, which on a reply is usually the signature of
the message being answered.

Once a citizen taps anything, the open set becomes theirs and the rule stops
having an opinion. That is the only behaviour that does not fight somebody who
is reading.

TWO: SEARCH IN MAIL.

Server-side, over subject, both names, both addresses and the body — the five
things a person actually remembers a message by. A client-side filter would
only ever have searched the newest page of one folder, and would have failed to
find a message the citizen is certain they have, which is worse than no search.

ANDed with the folder clause rather than replacing it. A search that silently
escapes the folder you are standing in is how somebody finds a message in Trash
believing they are in the Inbox, and replies to it.

Debounced at 250ms, and the needle is part of the query key — so a search is a
cache entry rather than a refetch, clearing the box shows the folder again
instantly, and `placeholderData` holds the previous rows so the list does not
flicker under somebody's hands while they type. An empty result says the search
found nothing rather than that the mailbox is empty; telling somebody with a
full inbox "no mail yet" is a lie the interface tells about itself.

The bar is the city's own carved well at a 999px radius, capped at 560px on a
desktop and full width on a phone. No new colour, no new depth, and Safari's
own clear affordance is suppressed in favour of one with a 44px target.

API tsc clean, jest 89/89 across 6 mail suites. Web tsc clean, vitest 437/437,
a11y 0, vite build clean.

MSG
echo "== committed"

echo
echo "==============================================================="
echo " Landed: $NEEDS — push and Railway + Vercel ship it."
echo "==============================================================="
